WEBVTT

01:25.630 --> 01:28.755
Come on, the sun is out. It's perfect.

01:29.338 --> 01:30.463
Come on, let's go.

01:30.546 --> 01:34.046
- Can you get up, please, please, babe?
- Mm, okay.

01:34.130 --> 01:36.713
Oh, babe, your breath.

01:37.796 --> 01:38.880
You love it.

01:40.588 --> 01:42.255
- Wake up.
- Okay.

01:42.338 --> 01:43.171
- Yeah.
- Hm.

01:43.255 --> 01:44.963
- Go away.
- Let's go. Yeah.

01:45.046 --> 01:47.213
- Leave me alone.
- Let's get going, come on.

02:10.130 --> 02:12.588
Hey! Easy now.

02:22.921 --> 02:24.963
Come on, old man. You got this.

02:38.088 --> 02:39.546
Damn, it's getting cold.

02:39.630 --> 02:41.713
That's just your Aussie ass.

02:47.213 --> 02:50.588
- You ready to get to the top?
- Not yet, baby.

02:50.671 --> 02:52.088
Let's go.

02:54.338 --> 02:56.296
Yeah! You got it.

03:09.630 --> 03:10.880
No rush.

03:17.380 --> 03:18.380
You're all good.

03:18.463 --> 03:22.630
It's the same goddamn spot every time.
Gonna be here forever.

03:22.713 --> 03:24.296
How can I help you?

03:26.463 --> 03:27.671
I'm good.

03:28.630 --> 03:31.130
I got this. I can...

03:31.213 --> 03:32.505
I can do this.

03:33.213 --> 03:34.630
Just take your time.

03:51.713 --> 03:53.213
Nice.

04:04.963 --> 04:05.963
What?

04:06.463 --> 04:08.046
I reckon we should call it a day.

04:08.130 --> 04:09.796
It's the final pitch, Tommy.

04:18.671 --> 04:20.505
It'll still be there
in the morning, I promise.

04:21.963 --> 04:24.630
Plus, there's a bit of shit weather
coming in. Have a look.

04:24.713 --> 04:26.255
Just give me one more try.

04:26.338 --> 04:28.796
We can both hit the top
and make tent well within an hour.

04:28.880 --> 04:30.963
I know we can do that.
I want to summit today.

04:31.046 --> 04:33.505
- That is exactly why--
- No, I want to summit today.

04:33.588 --> 04:35.838
That's exactly why
you have a climbing partner,

04:35.921 --> 04:38.546
so that someone can make the call
when one of you loses the plot.

04:39.713 --> 04:43.171
So I'm making a call. Okay?

04:43.255 --> 04:45.171
Sash, it's all good.

04:45.255 --> 04:47.630
It was beautiful climbing,
up until where you...

04:47.713 --> 04:49.005
Right until when it wasn't.

04:57.296 --> 05:00.255
Just wondering whether we should
take a rain check tomorrow, that's all.

05:00.338 --> 05:02.421
Are you kidding me?
It's just a little weather.

05:02.505 --> 05:04.505
What's... What's going on?

05:05.255 --> 05:06.505
No, just...

05:07.463 --> 05:11.213
I just feel like sometimes
you rush it a little bit, that's all.

05:21.838 --> 05:23.171
Anything else?

05:24.921 --> 05:29.171
I don't know how many more
of these trips I've got left in me.

05:29.255 --> 05:34.630
Look, don't get me wrong.
I love this. I love us. I love you.

05:34.713 --> 05:36.421
Stop it. You do this every time.

05:36.505 --> 05:39.171
You know, the climb gets tough,
and then all of a sudden,

05:39.255 --> 05:40.546
you start talking like this.

05:40.630 --> 05:42.505
No, I'm just talking about
slowing it down a bit,

05:42.588 --> 05:44.963
not doing so many extreme things.

05:45.046 --> 05:46.671
Oh my God.

05:51.005 --> 05:52.296
There's an old saying.

05:52.380 --> 05:54.421
Luck is like anything else
you take up the mountain.

05:54.505 --> 05:56.171
Eventually, it's gonna run out.

05:56.255 --> 05:57.880
You serious?

05:59.296 --> 06:03.088
You're gonna tell me your luck
has run out halfway up a mountain?

06:03.171 --> 06:05.046
If my lucky compass is saying I should--

06:05.130 --> 06:07.921
Oh my God.
Just stop with that fucking compass.

06:12.921 --> 06:14.338
I'm sorry, Sash.

06:15.921 --> 06:17.796
I'm just being a bit of a sook.

06:19.338 --> 06:20.421
Come here.

06:24.546 --> 06:26.255
Where does it hurt?

06:27.296 --> 06:28.296
Yeah, right there.

06:28.380 --> 06:30.005
- Right here?
- Yeah.

06:30.088 --> 06:33.380
Jesus.

06:34.880 --> 06:37.505
Promise me we'll be back
after the storm's passed.

06:37.588 --> 06:40.880
We'll get going first thing, okay?
I promise not to sleep in.

06:42.255 --> 06:44.630
Is that a date?

07:04.505 --> 07:07.296
- Get into the wall!
- Okay, okay, okay.

07:08.046 --> 07:09.505
Keep your head down.

07:14.880 --> 07:17.880
Okay. I want us to go down a little bit.

07:17.963 --> 07:20.380
It's a bit safer there
at that ledge, okay?

07:20.463 --> 07:21.546
Okay.

07:25.088 --> 07:26.630
- You all right?
- Yeah.

07:26.713 --> 07:28.255
You can go faster if you want.

07:28.338 --> 07:29.338
- Oh yeah?
- Yeah.

07:29.421 --> 07:30.880
Now you want me to go faster?

07:30.963 --> 07:32.796
- Yeah.
- All right.

07:40.838 --> 07:42.088
You safe?

07:46.505 --> 07:47.630
God.

07:53.963 --> 07:54.921
Are you okay?

07:55.005 --> 07:57.171
Tommy! Get down here!

07:57.255 --> 07:58.796
Did you tie a knot for this rap?

07:58.880 --> 08:00.088
Yeah!

08:03.421 --> 08:05.755
Oh shit! Tommy, wait!

08:05.838 --> 08:07.505
Just give me a sec.

08:07.588 --> 08:10.880
Tommy!

08:12.671 --> 08:13.588
No!

08:14.213 --> 08:15.671
Shit.

08:18.505 --> 08:20.171
Tommy!

08:26.421 --> 08:30.213
Tommy, wake up!

08:30.296 --> 08:32.963
You're dragging us off the mountain!

08:38.630 --> 08:41.546
I can't hold it any longer!

09:04.546 --> 09:06.963
Oh!

10:10.130 --> 10:15.880
And I'm back on Boogie Street

10:28.630 --> 10:30.671
A cigarette

10:32.838 --> 10:35.463
And then it's time to go

10:37.838 --> 10:41.796
I tidied up the kitchenette

10:43.463 --> 10:47.296
I tuned the old banjo

10:49.130 --> 10:54.713
I'm wanted at the traffic jam

10:54.796 --> 10:58.505
They're saving me a seat

11:00.463 --> 11:03.088
I'm what I am

11:04.005 --> 11:09.338
And what I am
Is back on Boogie Street

11:41.546 --> 11:44.880
It's just these climbs, man,
the big tough ones. It's just...

11:45.505 --> 11:46.880
Takes a lot of ego, you know?

11:46.963 --> 11:50.005
If you're nice,
I'll share some of my ego with you.

12:21.630 --> 12:22.963
- Hey.
- G'day.

12:24.755 --> 12:26.130
You going out alone?

12:27.130 --> 12:28.671
I wouldn't recommend it.

12:30.380 --> 12:32.588
People get lost in these woods
all the time.

12:32.671 --> 12:34.630
And here, they stay lost.

12:35.296 --> 12:37.130
Can you sign in for us?

12:39.505 --> 12:41.255
Just so we know where you're going.

12:51.130 --> 12:53.963
Tough luck. Tough luck. That's yours.

12:54.046 --> 12:55.755
That's the good stuff.

12:56.463 --> 12:58.421
That's the good shit, there.

13:00.671 --> 13:03.588
- Is that packed on?
- For you, it's quite packed on.

13:03.671 --> 13:05.713
- Here you go.
- All right, thank you.

13:05.796 --> 13:06.880
Take it easy.

13:09.088 --> 13:09.921
Hello.

13:12.796 --> 13:13.796
Hey.

13:23.296 --> 13:24.713
You got everything you need?

13:25.921 --> 13:28.546
- Hey.
- Look out. Here's trouble.

13:28.630 --> 13:30.671
How's it going, Mel? Ready for some more?

13:30.755 --> 13:33.255
Oh, yeah. It's selling like hotcakes.

13:33.755 --> 13:34.588
Oh.

13:36.046 --> 13:39.463
- Have you tried it?
- Get real. I wouldn't feed that to my dog.

13:39.546 --> 13:41.005
Well, I think your dog's missing out.

13:41.796 --> 13:42.963
Excuse me.

13:43.713 --> 13:44.796
Thank you.

13:45.671 --> 13:47.630
Don't you say "excuse me"
where you come from?

13:49.880 --> 13:51.796
Did you not hear me? I said thank you.

13:57.255 --> 14:00.296
Where are you heading?
We could be your guides.

14:00.880 --> 14:02.463
We know the place real well.

14:03.005 --> 14:05.671
- I'm okay.
- We're just trying to be nice.

14:05.755 --> 14:07.505
I think she's okay, fellas.

14:08.588 --> 14:10.671
Looks like she got everything she needs.

14:19.755 --> 14:22.130
Full tank on six.

14:25.046 --> 14:26.505
I'm sorry about that.

14:27.421 --> 14:29.755
I just thought
I should probably have a bit of a word.

14:29.838 --> 14:32.546
Yeah, you didn't need to. It's okay.

14:32.630 --> 14:33.755
Oh, okay.

14:35.005 --> 14:36.046
No worries.

14:37.463 --> 14:40.505
Thanks, Mel. I'll be back in a tick.
I'm just gonna bring the car around.

14:40.588 --> 14:42.630
Yeah. Sixty.

14:46.546 --> 14:47.546
Ta.

14:52.963 --> 14:54.755
Can you add this?

15:13.296 --> 15:14.755
Hi, hello?

15:14.838 --> 15:17.713
Hi. Um, can you...?

15:18.380 --> 15:19.671
Hey.

15:19.755 --> 15:21.880
I'm trying to get to Grand Isle Narrows.

15:21.963 --> 15:23.213
- Yeah?
- My GPS is out. Yeah.

15:23.296 --> 15:25.255
- You here for the canyon?
- Yeah.

15:26.380 --> 15:27.380
Yeah.

15:29.046 --> 15:31.005
You want the easy way or the hard way?

15:31.088 --> 15:33.380
Just... the best way.

15:33.963 --> 15:37.213
- Okay. So, this is us.
- Mm-hm.

15:37.296 --> 15:38.505
You make this left,

15:38.588 --> 15:40.880
then it's a bit of a dog leg,
then a straight 50Ks.

15:40.963 --> 15:42.380
Okay, that's easy.

15:42.463 --> 15:45.921
Sorry, can I give you my advice?
Completely different.

15:47.713 --> 15:49.296
Start at Blackstone Bay.

15:49.880 --> 15:50.880
Here.

15:51.380 --> 15:54.921
- You go about nine Ks.
- Mm-hm.

15:55.005 --> 15:59.046
Just before you get to the split break,
you'll find the most amazing camping area.

15:59.130 --> 15:59.963
Okay.

16:00.046 --> 16:02.546
It's a bit of a well-kept secret,
right by the shore.

16:02.630 --> 16:04.880
- Oh, thanks.
- You think you can handle that?

16:06.421 --> 16:07.796
Yeah, I think I can handle it.

16:07.880 --> 16:08.713
- Okay.
- Okay.

16:08.796 --> 16:10.796
You're gonna love it.
The water's unbelievable.

16:10.880 --> 16:13.005
Okay, great. I really appreciate it.

16:13.088 --> 16:15.338
Okay. Just one more thing to think about.

16:16.088 --> 16:19.171
You know... I hope you know what
you're doing, 'cause it can get intense.

16:19.255 --> 16:21.338
- Intense, I know. It's okay.
- Pretty gnarly.

16:21.421 --> 16:22.796
Most people do it in pairs.

16:23.796 --> 16:25.005
- I'm gonna go.
- Oh, okay.

16:25.088 --> 16:27.130
I wasn't suggesting that you and I do--

17:29.005 --> 17:30.088
Fuck.

17:32.088 --> 17:33.463
That's her again.

17:35.463 --> 17:36.921
Do you want a beer, love?

17:44.546 --> 17:46.463
I think she wants to be alone.

17:47.630 --> 17:49.213
You string up the little one.

17:51.296 --> 17:53.171
Oh...

17:54.880 --> 17:57.380
Oi! Hey, easy.

18:08.755 --> 18:13.005
- She's trying to get out.
- Sorry, no backing out now, love.

18:14.463 --> 18:15.755
I'm talking to you.

18:46.963 --> 18:48.963
We're just trying to be nice.

18:54.130 --> 18:55.130
Okay.

19:11.880 --> 19:14.296
You're missin' the best bits.

19:14.380 --> 19:16.671
That's what happens
if you stay in the car all day.

19:16.755 --> 19:19.046
- Look at this beautiful thing.
- Right.

19:19.130 --> 19:22.046
Okay, let's go.
Diesel, Ripper, get in the truck.

20:23.921 --> 20:24.755
Ooh!

24:54.380 --> 24:55.505
What?

25:00.130 --> 25:01.255
What the fuck?

25:04.338 --> 25:05.796
Where's my bag?

25:09.921 --> 25:10.921
Fuck.

25:19.255 --> 25:20.546
Fuck! Fuck!

26:55.130 --> 26:56.171
Hello?

27:14.671 --> 27:15.796
Hello?

27:18.713 --> 27:20.380
Ah! Hey!

27:21.005 --> 27:22.130
Hey.

27:22.213 --> 27:23.630
You made it!

27:23.713 --> 27:25.546
It's me, from the gas station.

27:25.630 --> 27:27.588
Yeah, I remember.

27:27.671 --> 27:28.546
I'm Ben.

27:28.630 --> 27:30.296
Sasha, Ben. Nice to meet you.

27:30.380 --> 27:31.588
Hi, Sasha.

27:31.671 --> 27:33.588
Hey, Blackstone Bay.

27:33.671 --> 27:36.171
What'd I tell you?
Dumps you right in the brown.

27:36.255 --> 27:38.630
- Mm-hm. Yeah.
- You having fun?

27:39.296 --> 27:41.380
Yeah, the runs are great. I just, um...

27:41.463 --> 27:45.088
Something got into my gear last night
and took everything. My phone, my food.

27:45.171 --> 27:48.046
Oh, bloody hell. That's no good.

27:48.130 --> 27:50.296
Your mobile phone bill's
gonna be through the roof.

27:51.421 --> 27:53.880
Yeah, it's the wombats.
They're texting all the time.

27:53.963 --> 27:55.171
They text constantly.

27:55.255 --> 27:57.796
Yeah, that's a little wombat paw
working the key,

27:57.880 --> 27:59.130
in case you hadn't noticed.

28:02.046 --> 28:05.296
Seriously, though, I'm sorry.
It's a drastic bummer.

28:05.380 --> 28:08.463
I thought I hung it up high enough,
but guess not.

28:08.546 --> 28:10.463
No such thing out here, I'm sorry to say.

28:10.546 --> 28:13.588
Good news is I always pack
twice what I need.

28:14.296 --> 28:16.630
- I'm more than happy to suit you up.
- Really?

28:16.713 --> 28:17.713
Yeah, of course.

28:17.796 --> 28:19.838
That's what you gotta do out here.
You gotta share.

28:19.921 --> 28:22.046
No other way we all stay alive.

28:22.130 --> 28:24.421
Thanks, Ben. That's really great.

28:25.463 --> 28:26.546
You hungry?

28:27.546 --> 28:29.380
- Just kinda looking for that gear.
- Sit down.

28:29.463 --> 28:31.213
- Let me get you some fish.
- I would really--

28:31.296 --> 28:33.421
Please, I insist. Sit down.

28:33.963 --> 28:36.130
- Okay.
- Yeah, just there. Take a seat.

28:36.213 --> 28:38.588
Eat some food, get the gear, and then go.

28:46.838 --> 28:48.630
Yeah, here we go.

28:49.713 --> 28:51.505
So you make beef jerky?

28:51.588 --> 28:52.796
Uh, yeah.

28:53.671 --> 28:56.380
Yeah, I make that myself.

28:58.255 --> 28:59.130
Cut it.

28:59.838 --> 29:00.880
Dry it.

29:01.713 --> 29:04.630
Hang it away from the flies
for a few weeks.

29:04.713 --> 29:06.005
Good protein.

29:07.338 --> 29:11.005
It's not bad. I had some last night.
It's actually really good.

29:11.088 --> 29:12.713
- You tried Jenno's?
- Mm-hm.

29:13.546 --> 29:15.421
Why "Jenno's," by the way?

29:15.505 --> 29:17.130
It was my mum's name.

29:18.296 --> 29:19.546
Named it after her.

29:19.630 --> 29:21.505
You named beef jerky after your mom?

29:21.588 --> 29:22.921
Yeah.

29:23.005 --> 29:25.755
Well, she must be really flattered.

29:29.380 --> 29:31.171
Water. Want something to drink?

29:36.505 --> 29:40.380
Ever seen this before?
It's water siphoned from a tree.

29:43.838 --> 29:45.171
Pretty cool, huh?

29:53.796 --> 29:56.505
Don't worry, I forgot to pack my roofies.

29:58.255 --> 30:00.005
Come on, you gotta hydrate.

30:01.588 --> 30:03.630
Yeah, got to hydrate.

30:04.338 --> 30:05.588
Oh yeah.

30:05.671 --> 30:07.796
That usually impresses people.

30:08.796 --> 30:10.213
Yeah, it's impressive.

30:10.296 --> 30:11.296
Right?

30:12.338 --> 30:13.171
Yeah.

30:14.630 --> 30:15.630
Okay, so...

30:17.713 --> 30:19.255
Spend a lot of time out here?

30:19.338 --> 30:22.213
Oh yeah.
Yeah, I practically live out here.

30:22.296 --> 30:26.296
It's like I'm in pain if I don't get out
on the river once or twice a week.

30:27.088 --> 30:29.005
It's almost physical, you know?

30:30.171 --> 30:31.255
That need.

30:32.255 --> 30:33.921
Where in Australia are you from?

30:34.005 --> 30:36.671
Technically, not from Australia.

30:36.755 --> 30:39.088
No, I come from somewhere
far less appealing.

30:39.671 --> 30:42.255
My mum brought me out here
when I was a kid.

30:42.338 --> 30:44.296
Let me guess. Britain?

30:48.046 --> 30:51.546
- Fuck off. I guessed?
- Yeah, you guessed right.

30:52.505 --> 30:54.796
Uh, how long you been kayaking for?

30:55.338 --> 30:56.171
Mm?

30:56.255 --> 30:58.421
Oh, just a while.
I do a little bit of everything.

30:58.505 --> 30:59.338
Ah!

30:59.421 --> 31:01.255
But mostly mountains, right?

31:03.463 --> 31:05.338
So, I already know about you.

31:06.338 --> 31:08.796
Yeah, you know,
the danger makes you feel alive.

31:08.880 --> 31:12.046
Gotta be in the moment, or you may die.
Perfection's the only option.

31:12.130 --> 31:14.588
All that bullshit
they tell people like us.

31:14.671 --> 31:17.255
Personally, I think
your wiring's just messed up.

31:17.338 --> 31:19.671
You can fight your way
through a lot of shit,

31:20.796 --> 31:22.213
but you can't beat your wiring.

31:23.755 --> 31:26.088
Ain't no mountain high enough, right?

31:28.421 --> 31:29.421
Here you go.

31:30.338 --> 31:31.505
I'm done with mountains.

31:32.713 --> 31:34.255
That's interesting.

31:35.213 --> 31:36.796
Let me guess.

31:36.880 --> 31:38.421
You broke up,

31:39.505 --> 31:43.546
and your boyfriend got the mountains,
and you got the rivers.

31:43.630 --> 31:45.130
Am I right?

31:49.213 --> 31:50.380
Oh shit.

31:51.255 --> 31:54.046
- I didn't mean to pry, Sasha. I'm so...
- No, it's fine.

31:54.130 --> 31:55.921
I was just trying to be funny. I...

31:56.421 --> 31:58.921
That's the cost
of spending so much time alone.

31:59.005 --> 32:02.380
You completely lose the ability
to function in polite society.

32:03.588 --> 32:05.963
I know what that feels like.
That's why I'm out here.

32:07.713 --> 32:09.880
Don't have to playact like a human being.

32:09.963 --> 32:13.921
Yeah. Yeah, there's enough noise
in the world, right?

32:14.005 --> 32:15.338
Speaking of noise,

32:15.838 --> 32:18.338
you know who showed up
at my campsite the other night?

32:19.213 --> 32:20.880
Those hunters from the gas station.

32:21.921 --> 32:23.713
They were definitely messing with me.

32:24.255 --> 32:26.130
Yeah, that's a little concerning.

32:26.713 --> 32:27.755
I know.

32:29.380 --> 32:30.755
Assholes.

32:31.755 --> 32:32.796
It's fine.

32:33.421 --> 32:36.130
You know, most hunters aren't like that.

32:36.213 --> 32:41.171
The good ones respect the wilderness,
and we make use of what we kill.

32:41.255 --> 32:44.296
It's not about having an excuse
to drink with your buddies.

32:45.046 --> 32:46.713
It's more reverent than that.

32:46.796 --> 32:49.255
- Yeah, they weren't reverent.
- No.

32:49.338 --> 32:50.796
They were trying to scare me.

32:50.880 --> 32:53.338
Yeah, no, it sounds that way.

32:55.338 --> 32:57.255
You handled them perfectly, though.

32:59.630 --> 33:00.463
What?

33:00.546 --> 33:02.963
You had grit and poise.

33:03.713 --> 33:06.796
Amazing. You didn't give them an inch,

33:06.880 --> 33:09.380
but you didn't give them
an excuse to hurt you either.

33:09.463 --> 33:11.130
I'm... I'm sorry, what are you saying?

33:11.213 --> 33:12.630
At the campsite.

33:13.255 --> 33:16.463
No, I was there.
I thought maybe you could use a hand.

33:16.546 --> 33:20.171
A woman alone and all.
Not the case, though, clearly.

33:23.713 --> 33:25.880
Nah, you're special, Sasha.

33:26.505 --> 33:27.880
Just like my mum.

33:29.130 --> 33:31.255
I could sense it the moment we met.

33:34.130 --> 33:36.338
You're not gonna finish your brekkie?

33:36.963 --> 33:39.213
- Would you like me to wrap it up?
- That's okay.

33:39.296 --> 33:41.463
I'm just gonna get out of here.

33:41.546 --> 33:43.213
Hey, Sasha, what?

33:46.713 --> 33:47.963
Right.

33:49.171 --> 33:50.088
Yeah, this.

